[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Missing specification-required scenarios leave contracted postconditions unexercised. First, node removal must purge incident prerequisite references as well as dependent references, and scheduler state synchronization must drop stale entries so state reporting reflects only nodes still registered after a removal. Second, deferred missing-dependency detection must also be exercised through the deterministic ordering operation, not only through whole-graph validation. Third, the longest weighted path contract must cover the empty graph, yielding an empty path and zero total weight. Fourth, dependency gating must cover a dependent with multiple prerequisites where one prerequisite has not yet completed, so the dependent remains pending instead of being promoted prematurely. Fifth, under CONTINUE_ON_ERROR, pending nodes that remain unblocked must stay eligible for execution, including a pending node whose prerequisites are already satisfied because it was registered after they completed, which must become ready. Sixth, completion reporting must also cover states where no ready nodes remain, for example after a mutation leaves only non-ready nodes or while a node is in progress, not only the empty-graph and all-terminal cases.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: Feedback fix for scheduler state synchronization: _sync_scheduler_states now drops stale entries for nodes no longer registered and initializes newly discovered nodes as READY when all of their prerequisite nodes have already SUCCEEDED (so nodes registered after their prerequisites completed become eligible), keeping model state/state reporting aligned with the removal-purge and dependency-gating contracts.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Addressed runtime feedback by exercising the missing contracted scenarios: (1) remove_node now verifies purging of both prerequisite and dependent incident references plus scheduler state reporting after removal; (2) topological_sort covers deferred missing-dependency detection; (3) compute_critical_path covers the empty graph (empty path, zero weight); (4) dependency gating covers a dependent with multiple prerequisites where one is unfinished, verifying it stays PENDING and is not prematurely promoted; (5) CONTINUE_ON_ERROR covers a late-registered pending node whose prerequisites already succeeded, verifying it becomes ready; (6) is_finished covers a node-in-progress non-terminal state and a graph with only blocked pending nodes. get_all_states also asserts reported keys match the currently registered nodes.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: test_topological_sort_rejects_deferred_missing_dependency (lines 497-500) asserts CycleError for a graph whose node 'a' references the unknown dependency 'ghost', which contradicts low/dag_engine_lite.pyi: DAG.add_node mandates that missing dependency existence checks be deferred to validate() and topological_sort() rather than eagerly raising, validate() POSTCONDITIONS require NodeNotFoundError when a dependency node is missing and reserve CycleError strictly for directed cycles, and DAGRunner.run Raises likewise lists NodeNotFoundError for referenced dependencies not present in the graph while CycleError covers only directed cycles; the author's # CHANGE correctly implemented this deferred missing-dependency check in topological_sort by raising NodeNotFoundError for the unknown reference, so the residual defect is the harness's unmandated expectation, and the test must assert NodeNotFoundError for the missing-dependency case instead of CycleError.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: Corrected deferred missing-dependency semantics in the model: topological_sort and compute_critical_path now raise NodeNotFoundError when a node references an unregistered dependency (per DAG.add_node's deferred-validation postcondition), reserving CycleError strictly for genuine directed cycles. This aligns model behavior with the contract and the implementation's deferred checks.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Fixed the deferred missing-dependency expectation: test_topological_sort_rejects_deferred_missing_dependency now asserts NodeNotFoundError (not CycleError) for a node referencing unknown dependency 'ghost', matching DAG.add_node's deferred-validation contract. The topological_sort and compute_critical_path overrides now branch on an SUT missing-dependency check before the cycle check, verifying NodeNotFoundError for unknown references and reserving CycleError for genuine directed cycles, so the exercised postconditions no longer contradict low/dag_engine_lite.pyi.
