[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: The remaining uncovered statements in this file are unreachable defensive branches that no conforming scenario through the contracted public operations can activate, so they must be restructured away or explicitly justified. Line 297, the missing-dependency skip inside the private cycle-detection helper, is unreachable because both contracted entry points that invoke cycle detection first raise the absent-prerequisite error, so cycle detection can never observe a dependency outside the registered node set. Line 522, the duplicate-visit skip inside the transitive blocked-dependent traversal, is unreachable because identifiers are already filtered against blocked dependents at enqueue time and the contract only requires transitive dependents of a failed node to reach the skipped terminal state, so no contracted scenario obliges the same dependent to be enqueued twice. Line 642, the empty-wave halt inside execution, is unreachable because completion reporting is contracted to report unfinished only while ready nodes remain, so a scheduler still reporting unfinished cannot yield an empty ready wave. Please eliminate these branches by restructuring, mark them with unreachable(), or annotate them with pragma no cover and an explicit assumption reason. No functional behavior change is requested.
